From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 19:16:54 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Physical page allocations come from sections of up to 2
 MiB (VICTORY_SECTION_MB, default 2; 0: one section as before)

One XMemAllocatePhysicalPages request was one pagefile section (the
title asks for 6.1 GiB at once), mapped 64 KiB at a time. Windows holds
a section's lock while views of it are mapped and unmapped, and so does
its worker that rebuilds large pages: the title's remaps waited behind
it (b44run1, in the world: a median 17.5 ms a frame, at most 1.3 s).
A request is now backed by sections of at most VICTORY_SECTION_MB MiB;
page numbers go on across them, and a run of pages stops where a
section does.

GPU side: sections are kept by handle in a map, a closed section's
handle is forgotten and our own view of it unmapped
(title_memory_section_closed), and the census counts sections by size.

Hand port of fork pull request #1274 (CuteBooty), itself after
RyanCase94's idea and first patch (fork #1089) and upstream #3177
(KainanP). Local: on by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
